  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2017-01-04",
   "text": "West Coast Ocean Protection Act of 2017\n This bill amends the Outer Continental Shelf Lands Act to prohibit the Bureau of Ocean Energy Management from issuing a lease for the exploration, development, or production of oil or natural gas in any area of the outer Continental Shelf off the coast of California, Oregon, or Washington."
  }
